[stderr] ---
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Establish layered unit, content, integration, and reserved browser-test
[stderr] conventions with isolated RNG, clock, and persistence fixtures. The harness
[stderr] must be repeatable and must never access real services or player data.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Dependencies
[stderr] 
[stderr] R0001 and R0002 are implementation dependencies. This contract may be authored
[stderr] and structurally validated before they run; its later implementation uses the
[stderr] shared seam from R0002.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Ownership
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Test-runner configuration and `tests/{core,content,platform,app}/fixtures`.
[stderr] - Deterministic fixture factories plus fake clock and RNG interfaces.
[stderr] - `docs/testing.md` and the reserved browser-test convention.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Behaviour
[stderr] 
[stderr] Provide factories that receive controlled clock, RNG, and storage fakes, reset
[stderr] their state between cases, and expose explicit deterministic inputs. Define
[stderr] separate layers for core, content, platform, and application checks so future
[stderr] features add evidence at the appropriate layer instead of coupling tests to
[stderr] real browser state or services.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Web and PWA differences
[stderr] 
[stderr] Shared fixtures cover core behaviour. Web and PWA adapter tests use isolated
[stderr] platform fakes; reserved browser tests are conventions only, not claims of a
[stderr] real browser/device matrix. PWA cache and web origin storage remain distinct
[stderr] from fixture storage.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Non-goals
[stderr] 
[stderr] Do not add final feature assertions, real browser or device compatibility
[stderr] claims, production telemetry, network calls, player data, campaign content, or
[stderr] product assets. Do not create incidental art, fonts, icons, audio, maps, or
[stderr] reference-derived fixture content.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Asset assessment
[stderr] 
[stderr] `asset_impact` is `not_applicable`. Fixtures contain only deterministic,
[stderr] non-product data and must not create incidental product assets or reserve them.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Verification
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Run a representative core fixture repeatedly and prove identical results.
[stderr] - Deliberately fail a fixture assertion and prove the runner reports it.
[stderr] - Verify fixture storage is isolated from browser-origin and production data.
[stderr] - Retain GATE-0002: this harness does not establish compatibility or
[stderr]   performance claims.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Evidence
[stderr] 
[stderr] Record repeated-run output, the deliberate-failure detection result, and an
[stderr] isolation check showing no real service, player, or browser-origin storage use.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Repeated execution of a controlled fixture returns identical results.
[stderr] - Fixture state, clock, RNG, and storage are isolated and resettable.
[stderr] - The harness defines layered conventions without asserting final features,
[stderr]   browser/device support, or production telemetry.
